# Which test of the reference compiler is answered by which test here.
#
# Four tab-separated columns:
#
#     <suite file>            the reference's, under shared/src/test/scala/sh/sysl (or jvm/…)
#     <case name>             the scalatest leaf, verbatim; `*` disposes of every case in the
#                             suite that has no line of its own. A name written in the source as a
#                             stripMargin literal spanning two or more lines -- `"""first line
#                             |the rest""".stripMargin in {` -- is NOT verbatim here: it is the
#                             source lines joined with a single space, each stripped of leading
#                             whitespace and of the stripMargin '|' marker. That is the same
#                             normalization `scripts/reference_test_inventory.sh` applies (its
#                             header has the worked example), so a row written by reading the
#                             source directly matches what the inventory prints.
#                             A case written inside a LOOP is one row per ITERATION, keyed by the
#                             name that iteration ran under (`reference_inventory.tsv`'s leaf
#                             column): `aarch64-macos sizes the array at 8`, never the template
#                             `$name sizes the array at $width`, which matches nothing. An
#                             iteration gets a row only where the test here demonstrably covers
#                             it -- a loop over the same set, or a test of its own -- so a
#                             template's count can only go up by somebody reading a body.
#     <disposition>           `tests_x.sysl:<function>`, `covered-by <sweep>`, or `n/a <reason>`
#     <provenance>            `verified` -- somebody read both bodies and they assert the same
#                             claim on the same input; `auto` -- the two names carry the same
#                             content words and nothing else was checked
#
# A reference case with no line here is UNMAPPED, which is what section 7 is driving to zero.
# `scripts/reference_test_census.sh` counts the columns and lists what is left.
#
# The 422 `auto` rows were seeded once, mechanically: content words of the two names (stop words
# and punctuation dropped), Jaccard at 0.6 or better, at least three content words on the
# reference's side, the destination confined to the three files of this repository the suite's
# whole wording points at, and each test here claimed by at most one case. Twenty were read by
# hand afterwards and one was wrong (`DerivingTests` "an opaque struct with no fields" against
# `a_struct_with_two_fields`), so expect about one in twenty of them to be.
#
# AN `auto` ROW IS A CLAIM ABOUT TWO NAMES AND NOTHING MORE. Whoever ports a suite reads its
# `auto` rows first, and every one of them ends the batch either `verified` or replaced.
#
# An `n/a` row needs a reason a reader can check. There are four of them.
#
